{
  "_comment": "First end-to-end demonstration of the cilock v0.3 BackRef graph (see https://cilock.aflock.ai/concepts/the-spine-of-the-graph) using attestationsFrom + a per-file inclusion-proof emitted by 'cilock prove'. Four steps — build, scan-syft, scan-trivy, release — where the release step's regopolicies pulls predicates from the three earlier steps via attestationsFrom and also pulls the inclusion-proof envelope via externalFrom (because inclusion-proof envelopes are bare-predicate DSSEs, not Collections). The Rego enforces (1) the inclusion-proof's treeRoot equals the build's product/v0.3 merkleRoot, (2) the syft SBOM has >= 1 component, (3) the trivy SARIF report has zero error-level findings. The committed module field is a static base64 of policy/rego/release-gate.rego — verify-recipe.sh re-renders it freshly at runtime so reviewers can edit the rego in plaintext.",
